The attached image compares the anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with different doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11. It shows that both AH and Nano-11 significantly enhance the antibody response compared to rPA alone. Specifically, Nano-11 demonstrates comparable or superior immunopotentiation to AH, maintaining high antibody titers even at a lower dose (12.5 µg/dose) where AH's efficacy is reduced, indicating its effectiveness as a vaccine adjuvant.